# BCT Delivery Flow

## Integration requests — coordination, not role authority

- Each project has an autonomous Manager and Workers. Managers own task
  breakdown, isolated development, review and readiness decisions. When ready,
  a Manager submits an integration request with exact repository/branch/SHA,
  test and CI evidence, affected files, target LIVE products, rollback details
  and a stable request/delivery ID. The authoritative BCT source remains
  local D:/BCT/source main; a GitHub feature branch is only for review/CI.
  Do not create another supervisor hierarchy or duplicate orchestration system.
- **Default integration stopping point for every project and individual Work:**
  Workers implement and test only in isolated worktrees, then return exact
  branch/HEAD/file/test evidence to their Manager. A Manager verifies the
  candidate and calls BCT `bct_integration_queue` operation `submit` once
  with a stable request ID. It records the returned monotonic `sequence`
  and reports `READY_FOR_INTEGRATION`, **not** main/LIVE/GitHub completion.
  The queue lives in BCT's existing runtime `state.sqlite` table
  `integration_requests`; consult `docs/INTEGRATION_REQUEST_QUEUE_V1.md`.
  Unless the user directly appoints an executor for actual integration,
  stop before local main merge, LIVE mutation and GitHub main publication.
  A direct user appointment still requires exact Work/Operation/resource
  conflict checks; it never grants a supervisor-only role.
- **Default route, not exclusive permission:** BCT durably records each request
  and ordinarily delivers one notification to the designated coordination
  ("supervisor") node. That node gathers requests, sequences conflicts, and
  delegates execution. Supervisor identity by itself grants **no** unique
  permission to commit, merge, deploy or publish.
- **User-directed route:** If the user tells a project Manager "you handle
  integration and deployment", BCT may route or reassign that exact request
  directly to that Manager. It does not require supervisor permission; record
  the new assignee, reason, revision and original request ID without replaying
  an already-submitted effect. Likewise, the supervisor may delegate a request
  to a Manager, subject to existing authenticated Work scope and operation
  receipts.
- **Single effect lane per repository:** Whichever authorized Work owner is
  assigned to execute must use existing BCT guarded operations. Before the
  first main-changing effect, acquire or verify one shared repository-scoped
  write reservation, exact main SHA and clean tree. An unrelated Manager
  holding the same repository's main integration effect must cause the next
  request to wait or return a concrete conflict, **not** a role-based denial.
  Products or independent Git repositories can be handled independently.
  LIVE publication similarly requires an exact per-target effect reservation.
- The coordination request and delivery ACK are **not execution success**.
  Keep request registration, routed message, ACK, claimed owner, merged SHA,
  verified test/CI receipt, deployed payload/running version, and published
  GitHub main SHA as separate durable stages. Duplicate delivery IDs are
  idempotent; UNKNOWN effects are investigated before any retry.
- **Normal delivery sequence:** isolated changes and focused regression ->
  exact candidate CI on a non-main GitHub branch -> request stored and routed
  to the coordinator (or user-designated Manager) -> eligible assignee obtains
  the shared write reservation -> guarded local-main merge -> exact resulting
  main verification and required CI -> guarded LIVE deployment and physical
  acceptance where applicable -> GitHub main fast-forward synchronization
  **last** -> reconcile completion evidence. Core, Monitor and RCC remain
  separate deployment targets and only affected targets are deployed.
- Recovery works without the original ChatGPT tab: pending requests, routing
  decisions and receipts belong to BCT's existing durable Work/Operation and
  orchestration state. Use existing RCC message/ACK and Manager Wake contracts
  when their exact session and recipient bindings apply; a CI Inbox entry is
  not a generic integration request. If no coordinator node is bound, retain
  the request for manual routing rather than inventing a destination.
- This rule expresses the intended workflow, **not** a proven OS-level lock.
  Direct generic execute, git_commit, write and deployment commands can still
  bypass a coordination convention. Evaluate their existing Work and resource
  fences before claiming machine enforcement, and do not grant or revoke
  permissions merely because a node is called "supervisor". The exclusive
  resource is the *current effect reservation*, not a permanent AI role.


Use this as the default for BCT changes unless the user explicitly narrows or
overrides the scope.

1. Before changing anything, record the intended files, permitted deployment
   boundary, E2E success criteria, and protected UNKNOWN operations/claims.
2. Complete the focused regression, relevant local suite, static checks, and
   diff check before any LIVE change. Use the full suite when the affected
   boundary or repository gate requires it; do not make a reversible display
   correction wait on unrelated shards.
3. Use one of two explicit delivery lanes and record which lane applies:
   - **Reversible local-display lane**: Monitor-only HTML/CSS/rendering changes
     which do not alter Core/RCC/Native Host protocols, browser state, stored
     data, claims, messages, credentials, or external systems may be committed
     on the local authoritative main after local gates. Create a rollback
     backup, then run exact-commit LIVE E2E through the currently assigned
     integrator's guarded BCT Work after the applicable candidate CI and
     source integration gate. The supervisor route is optional.
     Keep GitHub main synchronization after guarded LIVE acceptance, while
     allowing exact candidate CI on a non-main ref. The work is complete
     only after both LIVE E2E and required exact CI pass; a material display
     regression triggers the documented rollback decision.
   - **Effectful lane**: Core, RCC, Native Host, wire/schema/security, database,
     claim, Chrome mutation, message send, or other externally visible effects
     require exact-head CI success before LIVE deployment or E2E effects.
4. Keep a coherent correction and its regression coverage in one exact commit
   or PR. For the effectful lane, prepare deployment and rollback while CI runs
   without changing LIVE. For the local-display lane, never let LIVE and CI
   test different commits.
5. Advance effectful E2E only in order: deployment health, one round trip,
   durable receipt/recovery, then the larger orchestration scenario.
6. Use compact status or presence for routine health. Request full DOM or RCC
   state only for a diagnosis, and label stale or uncertain observations rather
   than treating them as IDLE.
7. On a failed external effect, preserve the receipt and collect evidence
   (canonical text, DOM, ACK, active execution, pending receipt) before any
   retry. Never replay an UNKNOWN effect or release a protected claim merely
   to make progress.
8. Parallelize read-only inspection, test preparation, and GitHub observation.
   Keep shared worktree writes, browser sends, and LIVE mutations serialized.

Report the final state with the exact tested SHA, test/CI evidence, LIVE
evidence, E2E result, and any deferred follow-ups.

## Completion semantics and durable continuation

- Treat the user's entire requested outcome as ONE acceptance scope. Do not present coding, modularization, PR, CI, local-main merge, package publication, or installed files as "완료" while actual running operation or user-facing acceptance remains outstanding.
- Only report "완료" after the requested change is applied, the exact running build and receipt are verified, real usage/E2E is accepted, and no requested part remains. If some steps are still open, state "진행 N/M", list the remaining concrete step(s), and avoid contradictory success language.
- Define the M concrete gates at the start from the full user request and keep the denominator stable. If the scope changes, explicitly rebaseline it with evidence; never invent stages to inflate progress.
- A stopped or blocked task stays visibly IN_PROGRESS/BLOCKED with its original durable Work ID, last verified SHA, receipts, next executable step, and precise blocker. Resume that same task first; do not create duplicate Work, ask the user to issue a copy-and-paste continuation prompt, or drift into old implementation paths.
- When an operation needs user interaction, distinguish the confirmed technical gate from remaining physical acceptance. Record user-observed success faithfully, without promoting unobserved components.

## Worktree lifetime and truthful Work state

- The only source authority is local `D:\BCT\source` on `main`; feature
  branches and worktrees are disposable *after* verified acceptance, not
  alternate canonical source copies. Name each feature worktree in the durable
  Work and receipt; avoid parallel writes to the shared main index.
- `Work.state=ACTIVE` is an authorization gate, **not** proof that execution
  is running or that user acceptance is incomplete. Derive execution status
  from operation receipts, running processes, and exact E2E/postconditions.
  Never mass-update Work states to FINISHED or erase UNKNOWN evidence to make
  a dashboard look clean.
- On a completed task, run the existing read-only
  `python scripts/bct_worktree_hygiene.py --repo D:\BCT\source --worktrees-root D:\BCT\worktrees --state-db D:\BCT\runtime\state\state.sqlite`
  before proposing cleanup. A REVIEW candidate is **not deletion approval**.
- To remove an exact accepted worktree, first verify it is on an ancestor of
  local main, clean including untracked/ignored files, not locked/detached,
  has no exact BCT Work/unfinished-or-UNKNOWN Operation/process references,
  and is not used by deployment/rollback or another ongoing task. Record
  branch, HEAD, before/after count, and the authoritative main SHA. Then use
  `git worktree remove <exact path>` **without** `--force`. Retain Git branch,
  commit, and durable receipts for recovery; never run broad prune/reset/clean.
- Any incomplete Git ownership check, missing Work ledger, ambiguous runtime
  reference, or user context that cannot be verified means HOLD, not cleanup.
- Before starting a new worktree, look for a suitable, owned, clean isolated
  worktree associated with the same Work; avoid unnecessary new worktrees.
